{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1474475-group-is-finally-running-it-s-aberrant-scion-crossover-and-we-ran-into-some-issues","id":1474475,"title":"Group is finally running it's Aberrant/Scion crossover, and we ran into some issues","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-11T21:44:37-08:00","id":1474475,"title":"Group is finally running it's Aberrant/Scion crossover, and we ran into some issues","content":"So we got our game session 0 out of the way, Our group of 5 players and the GM. 3 Novas, 2 Demi God's (for scaling purposes, it looks like they're around a similar power lvl) And we ran into quite a few minor hurdles. Like dealing with Aberrant vs Scion Scale (and how the numbers don't align quite evenly) and a few others.<br /> <br /> So I went on here, and tried to find if someone had already had this issue, but I couldn't find crossover discussion for these two any later than 2017.<br /> <br /> Has anyone come up with house rules dealing with stuff like this? I know the games weren't designed to interact right out of the box, but we weren't sure if someone had already done the work on what needs adjusting in order to make them fit each other as smooth as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T23:25:24-08:00","id":1474477,"title":"","content":"There really isn't a way to have them both be fair since a Nova can, out of the box, be as powerful as a full on deity with having Might Scale 6. It might be easier to adjust things from Scion to use Aberrant Scale. Like if something is Scale 4 for Scion, then you may want to beef that to like Scale 6 for Aberrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T02:32:24-08:00","id":1474490,"title":"","content":"My suggestion is to go all the way to one side or to the other (Aberrant has more solid rules, so its easier to push Scions to Aberrant side than the opposite), and build all of them under the same base rules.<br /> <br /> To bring Scions to Aberrant (and Trinity Continuum as a whole), create a template for each of the levels, (Hero, Demigod and God) to build on top of the basic character.<br /> <br /> They all would add Legend trait, Legendary Titles, Booms Callings and Knacks to the basic character (that would have Edges, skill tricks, etc).<br /> <br /> The knacks, booms and domains are not that hard to adapt, you just may need to fit scale properly (instead of Legend/2 rounding up, make it 1 + L/2 rounding up)<br /> Legendary titles add &quot;intensity scale&quot; when used, much like a Talent can do spending Inspiration, so basically you gain scale on your action, no matter action you are talking about, and it wont follow the same rules as Mega Attributes (so its easier).<br /> <br /> I agree with thedonnie about the power disparity, and its more than just the scale they can reach at full power.<br /> <br /> Scions are much more Legend points dependent than Novas to Quantum points, and Legend is far more difficulty to recover than Quantum, so you may need to balance the number of times a Scion may use minor sacrifices to something like 1/scene instead of 1/session.<br /> Try to keep Quantum lower than Legend, as the first is about 1/1 scale and Legend is 1/2. Demigods can stack scale, what gives them advantages, but its very Legend demanding, so a Nova may not get the same peak but have a better average. If you let quantum go free, than Demigods, and probably even Gods, have no chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T08:14:18-08:00","id":1474498,"title":"","content":"Also bear in mind that Scions are kind of like uber-Talents, in that everyone involved in the world of Legend has the ability to Twist Fate \u2014 which, conceptually, is equivalent to Dramatic Editing. Heroes, in fact, don't even have much in the way of \u201cuber-\u201d; they can be thought of as variant Talents, but with Legend, Boons, Callings, and Knacks instead of Inspiration, Facets, and Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T08:39:37-08:00","id":1474501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1474475-group-is-finally-running-it-s-aberrant-scion-crossover-and-we-ran-into-some-issues?p=1474498#post1474498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also bear in mind that Scions are kind of like uber-Talents, in that everyone involved in the world of Legend has the ability to Twist Fate \u2014 which, conceptually, is equivalent to Dramatic Editing. Heroes, in fact, don't even have much in the way of \u201cuber-\u201d; they can be thought of as variant Talents, but with Legend, Boons, Callings, and Knacks instead of Inspiration, Facets, and Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mindblowing moment! Scions are Talents! Demigods are Tier 3 Talents and Gods are Tier 4 Talents!<br /> <br /> Keep going with the discussion... It\u00b4s just some weird epiphany moment to me...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T10:22:07-08:00","id":1474506,"title":"","content":"That might be one way to go, yes. I'd be more inclined to say that: <br /> <br /> \u2022 Origins operates roughly at the Talents level:Twists of Fate are paid for by extra successes rather than a hard-to-earn currency like Legend or Inspiration; so even a \u201cbaseline\u201d person in the world of Scion can Twist Fate more readily than a Talent can DE. Also, where Talents have Inspiration-fueled Gifts, Origin level <b>Scion</b> characters (whether or not they're pre-Visitation Scions) have Momentum-fueled mortal Knacks. <br /> \u2022 Heroes are roughly on par with \u201cDark Star Novas\u201d: Feats of Scale can do much more than the \u201c+1 Scale\u201d that Talents can pull off, and aren't unlike Mega-Attributes, save for being thematically gated rather than gated by attribute; and in a mixed Scion/Aberrant game, I'd consider having Feats of Scale give a flat +Legend bonus to the appropriate Scale (in Scion, Scale tops of at 5; in Aberrant, it goes all the way up to 10). As well, they're able to pick up supernatural Knacks that are not unlike Mega-Edges. On the other hand, they start with two Purviews (a PSP and one from their parent); and note that the Purviews include Epic Dexterity, Epic Stamina, and Epic Strength, with Boons not unlike the Mega-Edges associated with Mega-Dexterity, Mega-Stamina, and Mega-Strength. And while there aren't any direct corollaries to the Mental and Social Mega-Attribute-based Mega-Edges, there are a number of Callings and Purviews that provide similar Knacks and Boons. What keeps Hero-level Scions from competing on par with regular Novas is their cap of no more than 4 Legend, and the need to channel any other Purviews through Relics or Guides. <br /> \u2022 Demigods, by contrast, ought to be roughly on par with regular Novas. A big change from Hero to Demigod is that Demigods have more options to Imbue Legend, which really takes the edge off of the Legend costs that pervade Scion: it's much easier when the Legend that you put into a Feat of Scale or a Marvel lets you perform it as many times as you'd like until you want to reclaim the Legend for some other purpose. On top of that, you have Casual Miracles and Dominion Stunts. <br /> \u2022 I cannot comment on how Gods compare to Novas, other than to note that they operate in the Legend 9+ range. Beyond that, <b>Scion: God</b> isn't it yet; so I have no idea what sorts of power upgrades they get compared to demigods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-12-2022, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T19:08:35-08:00","id":1474540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1474475-group-is-finally-running-it-s-aberrant-scion-crossover-and-we-ran-into-some-issues?p=1474506#post1474506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might be one way to go, yes. I'd be more inclined to say that: <br /> <br /> \u2022 Origins operates roughly at the Talents level:Twists of Fate are paid for by extra successes rather than a hard-to-earn currency like Legend or Inspiration; so even a \u201cbaseline\u201d person in the world of Scion can Twist Fate more readily than a Talent can DE. Also, where Talents have Inspiration-fueled Gifts, Origin level <b>Scion</b> characters (whether or not they're pre-Visitation Scions) have Momentum-fueled mortal Knacks. <br /> \u2022 Heroes are roughly on par with \u201cDark Star Novas\u201d: Feats of Scale can do much more than the \u201c+1 Scale\u201d that Talents can pull off, and aren't unlike Mega-Attributes, save for being thematically gated rather than gated by attribute; and in a mixed Scion/Aberrant game, I'd consider having Feats of Scale give a flat +Legend bonus to the appropriate Scale (in Scion, Scale tops of at 5; in Aberrant, it goes all the way up to 10). As well, they're able to pick up supernatural Knacks that are not unlike Mega-Edges. On the other hand, they start with two Purviews (a PSP and one from their parent); and note that the Purviews include Epic Dexterity, Epic Stamina, and Epic Strength, with Boons not unlike the Mega-Edges associated with Mega-Dexterity, Mega-Stamina, and Mega-Strength. And while there aren't any direct corollaries to the Mental and Social Mega-Attribute-based Mega-Edges, there are a number of Callings and Purviews that provide similar Knacks and Boons. What keeps Hero-level Scions from competing on par with regular Novas is their cap of no more than 4 Legend, and the need to channel any other Purviews through Relics or Guides. <br /> \u2022 Demigods, by contrast, ought to be roughly on par with regular Novas. A big change from Hero to Demigod is that Demigods have more options to Imbue Legend, which really takes the edge off of the Legend costs that pervade Scion: it's much easier when the Legend that you put into a Feat of Scale or a Marvel lets you perform it as many times as you'd like until you want to reclaim the Legend for some other purpose. On top of that, you have Casual Miracles and Dominion Stunts. <br /> \u2022 I cannot comment on how Gods compare to Novas, other than to note that they operate in the Legend 9+ range. Beyond that, <b>Scion: God</b> isn't it yet; so I have no idea what sorts of power upgrades they get compared to demigods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity how would you rate dragon character seeing as they work a bit more different compared to a regular Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T02:23:01-08:00","id":1474556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1474475-group-is-finally-running-it-s-aberrant-scion-crossover-and-we-ran-into-some-issues?p=1474501#post1474501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mindblowing moment! Scions are Talents! Demigods are Tier 3 Talents and Gods are Tier 4 Talents!<br /> <br /> Keep going with the discussion... It\u00b4s just some weird epiphany moment to me...</div> </div> </div> </div>My own crossover notes go with a slight alteration to this. Scions and Legendary Denizens are the opposite of Talents but are a paramorphs, like Assassins. Talents can subconsciously reach out and impose other realities on their but beings with Legend, while able to twist reality, are more limited in their Twists of Fate. But that is what makes them a breed apart. Fate forces probability down a path, like water flowing down in a groove. If Talents are free, the Legends are chained to Fate but those chains do have a benefit. Their power are focused.<br /> <br /> So yes, but no. Scions are like Talents, but more like Assassins and honestly, feel like they are further along that scale. Heroes are tier 2, thus the ones to compare to Talents and Assassins.<br /> <br /> Sidenote; I found it easier to use Scion's skill list (+ Enigma) for crossover, as it requires more effort to convert Scion's pantheons to work with Trinitiy's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T04:33:30-08:00","id":1474559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1474475-group-is-finally-running-it-s-aberrant-scion-crossover-and-we-ran-into-some-issues?p=1474556#post1474556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own crossover notes go with a slight alteration to this. Scions and Legendary Denizens are the opposite of Talents but are a paramorphs, like Assassins. Talents can subconsciously reach out and impose other realities on their but beings with Legend, while able to twist reality, are more limited in their Twists of Fate. But that is what makes them a breed apart. Fate forces probability down a path, like water flowing down in a groove. If Talents are free, the Legends are chained to Fate but those chains do have a benefit. Their power are focused.<br /> <br /> So yes, but no. Scions are like Talents, but more like Assassins and honestly, feel like they are further along that scale. Heroes are tier 2, thus the ones to compare to Talents and Assassins.<br /> <br /> Sidenote; I found it easier to use Scion's skill list (+ Enigma) for crossover, as it requires more effort to convert Scion's pantheons to work with Trinitiy's.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking much like that but didn't express me properly. Scions have a conscious control over fate, even if fate have control over them back, while talents are unconsciously controlling it.<br /> <br /> I am full of ideas and probably will write about it in the next few days to make it more solid. Lets see...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 02-13-2022, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T06:15:30-08:00","id":1474560,"title":"","content":"I would argue that Scions <i>don't</i> have a conscious control over Fate, anymore than Talents or Assassins do: their ability to Twist Fate is a subconscious manifestation; and the difference between what a mortal (i.e., Origins) can do when Twisting Fate and what a Hero can do is that a Hero's understanding of what's possible for him to achieve is much greater than a mortal's understanding. (Of course, that added understanding could be phrased as \u201cthe Hero knows that Fate is real\u201d; so\u2026)<br /> <br /> But yeah; I would say that Assassins are closer to Heroes than Talents are, in that Masteries can do the impossible just like Immortal Knacks, Boons, and Twists of Fate can. I'd still put them below Heroes, in that a Hero's ability to perform Feats of Scale is still far more impressive than the closest counterpart available to an Assassin; but that's still more impressive than what an Origins-level mortal can manage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T06:40:50-08:00","id":1474562,"title":"","content":"What I mean fate is more about their control over purviews and knacks.<br /> <br /> A Talent to get out of the limits of their condition would need to cross a barrier of system, much like a Inspiration 10 Stalwart is not a real Nova, but is as powerful as a Q1-2 Nova.<br /> <br /> Basically &quot;Legend&quot; would work for a Talent as Quantum works for Stalwart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T07:09:28-08:00","id":1474565,"title":"","content":"But Talents and Assassins already have Inspiration for that. That's part of why I'm thinking that Scions and their kind are <i>similar to</i>, but not <i>the same as</i>, Talents \u2014 unless you want to strip Talents out of the game entirely and <i>replace them</i> with Scions and their kind, which I could see doing. <br /> <br /> And if you do that, I could see using \u201cTalents\u201d to refer to Origin-level Scion-style characters, who lack a power stat like Legend or Inspiration, but can still access Dramatic Editing through the Stunts mechanic (i.e., Twists of Fate) and who have Callings and Knacks instead of Gifts. <br /> <br /> The only thing I <i>might</i> want to add to that would be an ability to spend Momentum for Dramatic Editing that's luck-based rather than skill-based \u2014 that is, to enable lucky breaks that don't involve the character taking any action at all. I'm not sure that's needed, though, as there usually are \u201cpassive\u201d skill checks that could be employed, like rolling to see if you notice what's around you: roll a basic success, and the Storyteller tells you about something there that you didn't already know about (or just says \u201cthere's nothing else here\u201d); roll additional successes, and you can modify that description as per the Dramatic Editing guidelines, with extra successes counting as Inspiration spent.<br /> <br /> (For TC:A!, I'd likely keep the Talent rules in place for stalwarts and mesmerists; but ironically not for daredevils. But we're discussing TC:Ab here, so it's something of a moot point.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-13-2022, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T11:33:59-08:00","id":1474576,"title":"","content":"On the skill list, most of the skills have a direct correlatio, you probably know them as most are just name changes, with a few exceptions.<br /> <br /> Occult becomes relevant in Scion, what takes one &quot;skill slot&quot;, so Humanities and Enigmas from TC becomes Academics in Scion.<br /> <br /> Now back to Talents x Scions. I am not trying to make a direct correlation between Inspiration and Legend, or Talents and Scions, I am just pointing that there are similarities enough to allow us to explore the mechanics. Knacks are related to Gifts, Masteries would look more like Immortal Knacks, as they are more activelly supernatural. Talents would be dependent on Supertech to explore some of their powers, what slowlly becomes less important as they grow in power (Demigods can use even places as sources of powers, what sounds much like Magic The Gathering, if you say like that).<br /> <br /> But yes, Talents are not Scions in any way, and Fate is not a real thing in TC, it's just a matter of both being mechanically linked to the idea of storytelling and not that much to any in game aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T13:31:12-08:00","id":1474581,"title":"","content":"My position here is that if you're trying to combine Aberrant and Scion, you could do worse than to yoink Talents and fill their spot with Scion: Origin characters. Then Heroes, Demigods, and Gods <i>would</i> be direct extensions of these \u201cTalents\u201d. Because if you don't know the underlying game mechanics, there's precious little difference between them. <br /> <br /> That said, I might also bring <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/321122\" target=\"_blank\">the New Gods</a>, or maybe the Atlanteans, into an Aberrant/Scion crossover \u2014 the latter being a nod to Jack Kirby's New Gods, and both being possible sources for Relics that could be conflated with Super-Science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T21:48:03-08:00","id":1474599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1474475-group-is-finally-running-it-s-aberrant-scion-crossover-and-we-ran-into-some-issues?p=1474560#post1474560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that Scions <i>don't</i> have a conscious control over Fate, anymore than Talents or Assassins do: their ability to Twist Fate is a subconscious manifestation; and the difference between what a mortal (i.e., Origins) can do when Twisting Fate and what a Hero can do is that a Hero's understanding of what's possible for him to achieve is much greater than a mortal's understanding. (Of course, that added understanding could be phrased as \u201cthe Hero knows that Fate is real\u201d; so\u2026)<br /> <br /> But yeah; I would say that Assassins are closer to Heroes than Talents are, in that Masteries can do the impossible just like Immortal Knacks, Boons, and Twists of Fate can. I'd still put them below Heroes, in that a Hero's ability to perform Feats of Scale is still far more impressive than the closest counterpart available to an Assassin; but that's still more impressive than what an Origins-level mortal can manage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is worse than that.<br /> In Scion, Twists of Fate are limited in scope to Paths, Titles and to a lesser extant Callings.<br /> <br /> While I agree Heroes tend to out perform Talents and to a lesser extent Assassins in their specialty, a better comparison is Stalwarts and Psions. Tier 2 includes a lot of options and parallels. The major difference is stamina; Heroes can hit bigger highs with scale but limited Legend points means that doesn't last long. Talents are generalists, like Psiads. Not built for the peak of power but more lateral options,<br /> <br /> Assassins are weird specialists, so do serve as a good point of contrast but Legends have a lot more bang and cover a wider area.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T06:56:15-08:00","id":1474622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1474475-group-is-finally-running-it-s-aberrant-scion-crossover-and-we-ran-into-some-issues?p=1474540#post1474540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of curiosity how would you rate dragon character seeing as they work a bit more different compared to a regular Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have much to say about them at the moment, other than that their design space overlaps heavily with <b>Assassins</b>: if I were bringing Heirs into a TC crossover game, I would put serious consideration into having them operate in the Shadow, the way Assassins do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T07:34:59-08:00","id":1474624,"title":"","content":"On Heirs, I would say they are in the exact position Assassins work, a kind of mystical space in the shadows hiding from the powers of the day light, so, with the exception of a few powers that are clearly &quot;Draconesque&quot;, Heirs are largely equivalent to Assassins.<br /> <br /> In the same way Heroes are Talents with some extra power and Demigods are largely Novas with a magical/divine theme.<br /> <br /> If you plan to use Dragons in a less spy more action game, then you may cross paths with other aspects, much like Heroes. A Dragon in a gave of heroes will be prety much working as a Hero, so it would fit a more a regular Talent+Psiad games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}